    },
    {
      "id": "5F6B0",
      "text": "$y=\\frac{2}{3} x$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/4uEs4--QOJdrfPRqL7lCdKIvKrBO-TAs5LlZ9A_BXlI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n$y=2 x-x^{2}, y=0, x=1$\r\nArea $=A=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 x-x^{2}\\right) d x$ or, $A=\\frac{2}{3}$ sq units\r\nLet $y=m x$ line divides area in two equal halves\r\n$\\therefore \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times \\mathrm{m}=\\frac{1}{3}$ or, $\\mathrm{m}=\\frac{2}{3} \\therefore$ equation of line is $\\mathrm{y}=\\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{x}$",
    "image": null
  },
